Q: How to get max length of a property using Entity Framework Core A: <p>Surprisingly, I couldn't find any Stack Overflow answer that answered this question (nor could Claude), while it's pretty trivial to do so.</p>
<p>For instance, by this extension method:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public static IEnumerable&lt;(string Name, int?)&gt; GetMaxLengths&lt;TEntity&gt;(this DbContext context)
    where TEntity : class
{
    return context.Model.FindEntityType(typeof(TEntity)).GetProperties()
        .Select(p =&gt; (p.Name, p.GetMaxLength()));
}
</code></pre>
<p>It returns the maximum length of any property as far as this length is configured in EF's metadata (mapping data), either by <code>MaxLengthAttribute</code>, <code>StringLengthAttribute</code>, or fluent mapping, such as</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>modelBuilder.Entity&lt;Test&gt;().Property(t =&gt; t.Name).HasMaxLength(10);
</code></pre>
<p>This is what the comment below the accepted answer hinted at.</p>

Q: Change image on scroll maintaining the rest of the page still A: <p>Using only CSS is somehow difficult; I actualy tried the best I ended up with this shot. This mainly uses animation-timeline: scroll() (still having Limited availability) and animation-range. (if using position:sticky slides don't move the same way as indicated website). I ended up adding remaining content in the last ' slide animation' to scroll with the previous and avoiding gap when separated. As far as I have seen what we can do with CSS these days I am sure somebody will be able to give a better full CSS solution.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.slider-container {
        height: calc(var(--tot) * 100vh);
}

.slide {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 100vh;
    z-index: calc(var(--tot) - var(--i));
}

.slide img {
    width: 100vw;
    height: 100vh;
    object-fit: cover;
}

.animation {
    animation-name: slide;
    animation-timeline: scroll();
    animation-duration: 1s;
    animation-fill-mode: both;

    animation-range: 
        calc(var(--i) * 100% / var(--tot)) 
        calc((var(--i) + 1) * 100% / var(--tot));
}

@keyframes slide {
    from {
        transform: translateY(0%);
    }
    to {
        transform: translateY(-100%);
    }
}</code></pre>
